=== kill-ring-across-readline-calls
tags: yank
--- script
readline "> " 2
--- keys
hello\C-a\C-k\r\C-y<dump>\r

=== kill-text-api
tags: rl_kill_text api
--- script
def k
rl_kill_text 1 4
set rl_point 1
dump
end
defun do-kill k
rl_bind_keyseq "\C-xk" do-kill
readline "> "
--- keys
abcdef\C-xk\C-e\C-y<dump>\r

=== kill-text-api-reversed
tags: rl_kill_text api
--- script
def k
rl_kill_text 4 1
set rl_point 1
dump
end
defun do-kill k
rl_bind_keyseq "\C-xk" do-kill
readline "> "
--- keys
abcdef\C-xk\C-e\C-y<dump>\r

=== kill-text-api-append
tags: rl_kill_text api
--- script
def k
rl_kill_text 0 2
set rl_point 0
set rl_last_func kill-word
end
defun do-kill k
rl_bind_keyseq "\C-xk" do-kill
readline "> "
--- keys
abcdef\C-xk\C-xk<dump>\C-y<dump>\r

=== kill-region-with-mark-at-zero-length
tags: kill-region
--- inputrc
"\C-xr": kill-region
--- keys
abc<pause>\C-@\C-xr<dump>\r

=== typeahead-insert-keeps-kill-chain
description: quirk: characters inserted as one typeahead batch do not reset rl_last_func, so two kills separated by such typing are merged
tags: unix-line-discard quirk typeahead
keys: a1\C-ua2\C-u\C-y<dump>\M-y<dump>\r

=== separate-kills-with-pause
tags: unix-line-discard yank-pop
keys: a1\C-u<pause>a2<pause>\C-u\C-y<dump>\M-y<dump>\r
